# 89. Final Review Questions

Before completing any meaningful change, ask:

```text
Does this satisfy the requirement?

Does it follow the architecture?

Does it follow the existing project patterns?

Did I reuse existing code where appropriate?

Did I introduce unnecessary complexity?

Did I validate external input?

Did I consider authorization?

Did I add tests?

Did I update documentation?

Did I consider responsive behavior?

Did I consider accessibility?

Did I consider i18n?

Did I consider performance?

Did I consider Cloudflare runtime behavior?

Did I inspect the final diff?

Does the build pass?
```

---

# 90. Final Workflow Principles

Always prefer:

```text
Understand
    over
Assume

Existing Patterns
    over
New Patterns

Documented Decisions
    over
Implicit Decisions

Small Changes
    over
Large Unrelated Changes

Validated Input
    over
Trusted Input

Tests
    over
Manual Assumptions

Root Cause
    over
Symptoms

Simple Architecture
    over
Overengineering

Focused Commits
    over
Large Mixed Commits

Measured Performance
    over
Premature Optimization

Server-side Security
    over
Client-side Assumptions

Accessible UI
    over
Visual-only Implementation

Reproducible Deployment
    over
Manual Deployment

Verified Completion
    over
"It Works on My Machine"
```

The goal of the workflow is not to slow development down.

The goal is to make Formly development predictable, testable, maintainable, secure, and easy to reason about.

Use the smallest workflow appropriate for the task, but never skip requirements that affect correctness, security, architecture, or production reliability.
